# Practical: Automate Maven Build Process with Jenkins Pipeline

We'll build on the **GitHub + Jenkins** practical you just completed.

The workflow will be:

```text
GitHub
   ↓
Jenkins
   ↓
Checkout Java/Maven project
   ↓
Maven compile
   ↓
Maven test
   ↓
Maven package
   ↓
SUCCESS
```

Jenkins recommends defining the Pipeline in a `Jenkinsfile` stored with the source code. [Jenkins Pipeline documentation](https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

## Step 1 — Install Java

Maven requires Java.

Check whether Java is already installed:

```bash
java -version
```

You should see something like:

```text
java version "17..."
```

If Java isn't installed, install a supported JDK and then check again.

Also check:

```bash
javac -version
```

---

# Step 2 — Install Maven

Download Maven from the official Apache Maven website:

[Apache Maven](https://maven.apache.org/download.cgi?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

After installation, check:

```bash
mvn -version
```

You should see something similar to:

```text
Apache Maven 3.x.x
Java version: 17...
```

If both commands work:

```bash
java -version
mvn -version
```

your computer is ready.

